  "id": "Compound::DB00833 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Cefaclor, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to Slc15a1, a protein involved in the transport of oligopeptides and peptides in a proton-dependent manner. This binding is linked to the participation of Slc15a1 in multiple transport activities, including peptide-proton symport, which is critical for the movement of charged peptides across cellular membranes. The evidence suggests that Cefaclor may influence the function of Slc15a2 through its interaction with Slc15a1, potentially modulating the transport of peptides by altering the activity of the Slc15a1 protein. The shared involvement of Slc15a1 in different transport mechanisms implies that Cefaclor could exert a regulatory effect on Slc15a2 by interacting with the same or related transport pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc15a1 as a central mediator in the cellular response to Cefaclor, suggesting a possible mechanism by which the drug affects cellular transport processes.",
